  "limitations": [
    "Exploratory timings on one shared workstation with three alternating warm observations per operation. Absolute timings varied between runs and do not establish a general benchmark.",
    "Cache control disables both embedding/reference admission and prediction-factory reuse; gains measure the combined optimization, not isolated prompt encoding.",
    "Batch2 did not improve measured throughput: generation was slower, editing effectively equal. Default batch_size remains 1.",
    "Preserving singleton seed draws does not guarantee identical serial/batch pixels. Real batch2 PNGs differed from serial, with mean absolute pixel error about 0.69-1.22 on an 8-bit channel scale; repeated batches were byte-identical.",
    "Batch4 was generated at 256x256, not at maximum supported dimensions. Batch memory admission is an estimate, not a proof of universal fit.",
    "Reference edit measurements used one 512x512 reference PNG. Multiple-reference batching and 9B/9B-KV checkpoints have no real generation proof.",
    "The dedicated FLUX.2 9B-KV denoising reference-cache path remains installed-API and tiny mocked-component tested only; ordinary 4B/9B do not enable it.",
    "Legacy Qwen-Image prompt caching is disabled due to ambiguous native positive/negative keys. Qwen-Image-2.1 and remaining families lack a real performance test.",
    "Fresh full-model calibrated quantization and remaining untested operations retain the limits recorded in image-models.md. No missing weights were downloaded.",
    "Timing medians and portable-driver proof preceded the final specialization-bound fix. The subsequent real B1/B2/B1 and aspect-ratio checks preserved all previous PNG hashes and retained one prediction signature; changed shapes now rebuild, with additional tracing cost. Stable-shape speedups remain workload-specific observations."
  ],
